From 734aeb60ff858976cdb36347ea5bf57bd94d5834 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ccicnce113424 <ccicnce113424@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 18:23:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/12] maintainers/scripts/nvidia-source-hashes: add a per-URL
 hash verifier

The script walks linuxPackages.nvidiaPackages, takes every component whose .src
is a fixed-output fetch, and builds one salted single-URL derivation per URL, so
each link is downloaded and checked against the declared hash on its own.
Platform specific sources come from an evaluation for each supported platform,
with only the URL and the hash transplanted onto the host derivation, which
covers the 32-bit and aarch64 hashes without a builder for them. --prefetch
prints the hashes a URL serves.

A URL that is not published yet does not fail the run, because GitHub and NVIDIA
publish a release at different times; --strict makes it fail.

Assisted-by: omp:DeepSeek V4.1 Flash
---
 .../scripts/nvidia-source-hashes/default.nix  | 367 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../scripts/nvidia-source-hashes/verify.sh    | 307 +++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 674 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 maintainers/scripts/nvidia-source-hashes/default.nix
