+- `hardware.nvidia.package` now takes a branch from `nvidiaPackages`; setting a
+  driver package fails the type check. Configurations that read the driver's
+  outputs need `.driver`:
+
+  ```diff
+  -environment.systemPackages = [ config.hardware.nvidia.package ];
+  +environment.systemPackages = [ config.hardware.nvidia.package.driver ];
+  ```
+
+  The kernel module moved to the new `hardware.nvidia.kernelModules` option,
+  which follows `package` and `hardware.nvidia.open` by default.
+
+- The driver packages are in `pkgs.nvidiaPackages.<branch>.driver` and no
+  longer need a kernel package set. The `nvidia_x11*` and `nvidia_dc` names
+  under `linuxPackages` keep their tools and modules and warn. For the kernel
+  modules use `.mod` or `.open` on the branch.
+
+- `linuxPackages.nvidiaPackages.mkDriver` now requires
+  `modprobeSha256`: nvidia-modprobe ships with the driver branch. The open
+  kernel module sources are fetched through `fetchFromGithubOrNvidia` now, so
+  their hashes had to be recomputed as well, and the `fetchOpenFromNvidia`
+  switch is gone. A declaration that omits `modprobeSha256` fails with a message
+  saying so.
+
+  ```diff
+    hardware.nvidia.package = config.boot.kernelPackages.nvidiaPackages.mkDriver {
+      version = "595.104.02";
+      sha256_64bit = "…";
+  -   openSha256 = "…";          # must be recomputed, `postFetch` now always applies
+  +   openSha256 = "…";
+  +   modprobeSha256 = "…";      # nvidia-modprobe now ships with the branch
+      …
+    };
+  ```
