From aad13dcfc79856bdde58cf618861d80aff6900a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ccicnce113424 <ccicnce113424@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 23:43:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] nvidia: update the consumers of the driver namespace

hardware.nvidia.package is a branch scope now, and the driver packages live in
pkgs.nvidiaPackages rather than pkgs.linuxPackages.nvidiaPackages, so every
consumer has to name the driver it wants instead of using the option as the
package.

The nvidia_x11 aliases in linux-kernels.nix still work and return the branch's
driver, with the tools and kernel modules in its passthru, so a package that
only wanted the driver needs no change. The adjustments here are the ones that
read an output, the kernel modules, or a tools entry off the old shape. The
boot.extraModulePackages example in system/boot/kernel.nix and the
boot.kernelPackages description used an alias whose name no longer says where
the module lives.

Assisted-by: omp:Space Bunny Alpha
